n input and one fed the Sasha input, with a policy that maps inputs to actions in a symmetric prisoner's dilemma. I'm weighing how my utility as Rowan, measured as negative years, would look when I evaluate policies from a vantage point before knowing which role I occupy.\n\nI'm checking the payoffs: symmetric pass-pass gives 2 years, submit-submit gives 4, and the asymmetric split averages 2.5 across the two roles. Since I don't yet know which role I'll occupy, the prior-based choice favors pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9057,"completion_tokens":863,"total_tokens":9920,"cost":0.053488,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.053488,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.036228,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01726},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":556,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}